<description>&lt;p&gt;María Corina Machado has returned from exile to Venezuela, prompting protests demanding elections and her continued presence. The United States has deployed Space Force electromagnetic and electronic warfare systems against Venezuela and pressured Reliance to refine Venezuelan oil, while CIA Director Ratcliffe visited Havana with a paramilitary operative linked to a past operation that killed 32 Cuban soldiers. The Pentagon has barred DoD personnel from using nonpublic information to bet on U.S. actions involving Venezuela, leading to the DOJ arrest of a soldier who made $400,000 betting on Maduro's removal. A bomb blast near the Colombia-Venezuela border injured at least four police officers, and a separate explosive attack on the same border injured six, including four officers. 2 battle-related deaths were recorded in 2007, according to UCDP.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Machine-written from the linked sources, checked for figures and names not in them.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;Al Jazeera&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;New York Post&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiiAFBVV95cUxQN1RPNGRmY3VhQkZ3TkRJSmVLQnk4eHhDOTFkdERzNUJKRE16cFVmZXJLVGVNSW1rbnBqeEtoY1dycmlJZHhtRWhubUZUT3hpaDRya2FodWZtcHIyVDhBRF9XR1dyLU9NRi1oOGRvQ3E1NlRzeHk1UEpncVUzemktYk5qTWtWYk9v?oc=5&quot;&gt;Latin Times&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMijgFBVV95cUxOcEJvTG9xaVA5QV9lN3ZQWGp6Vnk5ZW9FbU9iQm51VkFBc1pUcm9ZYlpfbGRaYVRuN0hlR3BsM3l2LXQ4enB2ajBUcDdSM2M1ZlRmSVM4ZTBXVExnUllrNmxiR29EdWlvbDZxb1l2T0M2a1dvWFg3SWhraHQ3YVdqQi13TGhZUFBua29oWlpR?oc=5&quot;&gt;AOL.co.uk&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMinwFBVV95cUxPeDRFd1BjOGlseHJrbF8tWjZsUGdOM0xkclZqZXo2aG8wbWpyNUxIUnI1cWNZYWZUWUptclgzZW1wYzJMSk5zaEFjbFp2VzlaamtNLVp3T3pQY0VKemNwZE9ZdWMzNW1QTTFEVEdnWnl3SlJBejRla005QldZdFhmMjZIR1pXNGQ0MUxLaWRvdmxxdnFRNU5z